    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-1994-sec-26",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "26 Section 26",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-1994#sec-26"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-1994.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-1994.pdf, p.12",
      "values:originalText": "Section 14 of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by omitting from subsection (1) \"will\" and substituting \"may\";\n(b) by omitting from subsection (6) \"Where\" and substituting \"Subject\nto subsections (8A) and (9), if\";\n(c) by inserting after subsection (8) the following subsection:\n\"(8A) Despite subsection (6), the Attorney-General is not required\nto make an order for the transfer of a prisoner under that subsection\nfrom New South Wales to another State or to a Territory if:\n(a) the prisoner has been removed to New South Wales under the\nRemoval of Prisoners (Australian Capital Territory) Act 1968;\nand\n(b) the prisoner has not applied for an order declaring him or her\nto be an exempt prisoner but, if he or she had so applied, the\nAttorney-General would have made such an order.\".\nFederal sentences—reductions and remissions",
      "skos:definition": "Section 14 of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by omitting from subsection (1) \"will\" and substituting \"may\";\n(b) by omitting from subsection (6) \"Where\" and substituting \"Subject\nto subsections (8A) and (9), if\";\n(c) by inserting after subsection (8) the following subsection:\n\"(8A) Despite subsection (6), the Attorney-General is not required\nto make an order for the transfer of a prisoner under that subsection\nfrom New South Wales to another State or to a Territory if:\n(a) the prisoner has been removed to New South Wales under the\nRemoval of Prisoners (Australian Capital Territory) Act 1968;\nand\n(b) the prisoner has not applied for an order declaring him or her\nto be an exempt prisoner but, if he or she had so applied, the\nAttorney-General would have made such an order.\".\nFederal sentences—reductions and remissions",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-1994-sec-26-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "8f91cdedc3d8aa443af424b33ea379be5e5bc10f8ca97ffb9085ab475cf471c8",
      "skos:note": "Attorney-General is not required to make an order for the transfer of a prisoner under subsection (6) from New South Wales to another State or to a Territory."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-1994#sec-26",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "26 Section 26",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 12,
      "values:originalText": "Section 14 of the Principal Act is amended:\n(a) by omitting from subsection (1) \"will\" and substituting \"may\";\n(b) by omitting from subsection (6) \"Where\" and substituting \"Subject\nto subsections (8A) and (9), if\";\n(c) by inserting after subsection (8) the following subsection:\n\"(8A) Despite subsection (6), the Attorney-General is not required\nto make an order for the transfer of a prisoner under that subsection\nfrom New South Wales to another State or to a Territory if:\n(a) the prisoner has been removed to New South Wales under the\nRemoval of Prisoners (Australian Capital Territory) Act 1968;\nand\n(b) the prisoner has not applied for an order declaring him or her\nto be an exempt prisoner but, if he or she had so applied, the\nAttorney-General would have made such an order.\".\nFederal sentences—reductions and remissions"
    },
