    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-1994-sec-29",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29 Section 29",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-1994#sec-29"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-1994.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-1994.pdf, p.13",
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this section:\n\"ACT\" means the Australian Capital Territory;\n\"ACT Act\" means the Prisoners (Interstate Transfer) Act 1994 of the\nAustralian Capital Territory;\n\"ACT prisoner\" has the same meaning as in the ACT Act;\n\"first step\" means:\n(a) the receipt by the Attorney-General of an application for a welfare\ntransfer order under section 6 of the Principal Act;\n(b) the receipt by the Attorney-General of a request for the making of a\ntrial transfer order under section 8 or 9 of the Principal Act;\n(c) the making by the Attorney-General on his or her own motion of an\napplication for a trial transfer order under section 8 or 9 of the\nPrincipal Act;\n(d) the service of a notice under subsection 14(1) of the Principal Act;\n(e) the making of an order under subsection 16(1) of the Principal Act;\n(f) the service of a notice under subsection 16A(1) of the Principal Act;\n\"joint prisoner\" has the same meaning as in the ACT Act;\n\"State\" includes the Northern Territory;\n\"transfer\" means a transfer or proposed transfer under the Principal Act.\n(2) In this section, a reference to a transfer between the ACT and a State\nincludes a reference to a transfer between New South Wales and a State if\nthe relevant prisoner is serving a sentence of imprisonment in New South\nWales under section 4 of the Removal of Prisoners (Australian Capital\nTerritory) Act 1968.\n(3) The amendments made by sections 25 and 28 do not apply to the\ntransfer of an ACT prisoner or a joint prisoner between the ACT and a State\nif at the time of the first step:\n(a) the Minister has not declared the ACT Act to he the State transfer law\nof the ACT under section 5 of the Principal Act; or\n(b) the relevant State Governor has not declared the ACT Act to he an\ninterstate law for the purposes of the State transfer law of that State;\nor\n\nCrimes and Other Legislation Amendment No. 182, 1994\n(c) the relevant ACT Minister has not declared that a law of that State\nis an interstate law for the purposes of the ACT Act.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) In this section:\n\"ACT\" means the Australian Capital Territory;\n\"ACT Act\" means the Prisoners (Interstate Transfer) Act 1994 of the\nAustralian Capital Territory;\n\"ACT prisoner\" has the same meaning as in the ACT Act;\n\"first step\" means:\n(a) the receipt by the Attorney-General of an application for a welfare\ntransfer order under section 6 of the Principal Act;\n(b) the receipt by the Attorney-General of a request for the making of a\ntrial transfer order under section 8 or 9 of the Principal Act;\n(c) the making by the Attorney-General on his or her own motion of an\napplication for a trial transfer order under section 8 or 9 of the\nPrincipal Act;\n(d) the service of a notice under subsection 14(1) of the Principal Act;\n(e) the making of an order under subsection 16(1) of the Principal Act;\n(f) the service of a notice under subsection 16A(1) of the Principal Act;\n\"joint prisoner\" has the same meaning as in the ACT Act;\n\"State\" includes the Northern Territory;\n\"transfer\" means a transfer or proposed transfer under the Principal Act.\n(2) In this section, a reference to a transfer between the ACT and a State\nincludes a reference to a transfer between New South Wales and a State if\nthe relevant prisoner is serving a sentence of imprisonment in New South\nWales under section 4 of the Removal of Prisoners (Australian Capital\nTerritory) Act 1968.\n(3) The amendments made by sections 25 and 28 do not apply to the\ntransfer of an ACT prisoner or a joint prisoner between the ACT and a State\nif at the time of the first step:\n(a) the Minister has not declared the ACT Act to he the State transfer law\nof the ACT under section 5 of the Principal Act; or\n(b) the relevant State Governor has not declared the ACT Act to he an\ninterstate law for the purposes of the State transfer law of that State;\nor\n\nCrimes and Other Legislation Amendment No. 182, 1994\n(c) the relevant ACT Minister has not declared that a law of that State\nis an interstate law for the purposes of the ACT Act.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-1994-sec-29-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-1994-sec-29-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-1994-sec-29-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "57ceaff3da28e5256fcb976a251e6a82e2d1797085622101366625a072f8df6a"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/crimes-and-other-legislation-amendment-act-1994#sec-29",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29 Section 29",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 13,
      "values:originalText": "(1) In this section:\n\"ACT\" means the Australian Capital Territory;\n\"ACT Act\" means the Prisoners (Interstate Transfer) Act 1994 of the\nAustralian Capital Territory;\n\"ACT prisoner\" has the same meaning as in the ACT Act;\n\"first step\" means:\n(a) the receipt by the Attorney-General of an application for a welfare\ntransfer order under section 6 of the Principal Act;\n(b) the receipt by the Attorney-General of a request for the making of a\ntrial transfer order under section 8 or 9 of the Principal Act;\n(c) the making by the Attorney-General on his or her own motion of an\napplication for a trial transfer order under section 8 or 9 of the\nPrincipal Act;\n(d) the service of a notice under subsection 14(1) of the Principal Act;\n(e) the making of an order under subsection 16(1) of the Principal Act;\n(f) the service of a notice under subsection 16A(1) of the Principal Act;\n\"joint prisoner\" has the same meaning as in the ACT Act;\n\"State\" includes the Northern Territory;\n\"transfer\" means a transfer or proposed transfer under the Principal Act.\n(2) In this section, a reference to a transfer between the ACT and a State\nincludes a reference to a transfer between New South Wales and a State if\nthe relevant prisoner is serving a sentence of imprisonment in New South\nWales under section 4 of the Removal of Prisoners (Australian Capital\nTerritory) Act 1968.\n(3) The amendments made by sections 25 and 28 do not apply to the\ntransfer of an ACT prisoner or a joint prisoner between the ACT and a State\nif at the time of the first step:\n(a) the Minister has not declared the ACT Act to he the State transfer law\nof the ACT under section 5 of the Principal Act; or\n(b) the relevant State Governor has not declared the ACT Act to he an\ninterstate law for the purposes of the State transfer law of that State;\nor\n\nCrimes and Other Legislation Amendment No. 182, 1994\n(c) the relevant ACT Minister has not declared that a law of that State\nis an interstate law for the purposes of the ACT Act."
    },
